# Design motion reference

Always consult before CSS/UI polish or animation work.

## Reference assets

- `detailing-app/design-references/invoice-fly/` — 218 ScreenDesigns replay frames (webp)
- `detailing-app/design-references/MOTION_SPEC.md` — archetypes + spec template
- `detailing-app/design-references/STYLE_PLAN.md` — phased polish plan (read before implementing)
- `detailing-app/docs/ui-css-audit.md` — CSS pattern owners (extend, don't duplicate)
- `detailing-app/src/app/tokens.css` — surfaces + motion tokens

## How to read animations (user cannot paste motion)

ScreenDesigns replays = sequential webp frames. To understand a motion:

1. User @-attaches 3–5 consecutive frames (start / mid / end), OR cites frame IDs
2. Read `invoice-fly/README.md` screen index for tagged ranges
3. Map to an archetype from `MOTION_SPEC.md`

## 12 motion archetypes (cover ~95% of Invoice Fly)

`sheet-enter` · `sheet-exit` · `list-stagger` · `press-depth` · `pill-spring` ·
`progress-fill` · `success-pop` · `tab-active` · `swipe-reveal` · `empty-enter` ·
`counter` · `attention-pulse`

Full definitions: `detailing-app/design-references/MOTION_SPEC.md`

## Motion spec template (when frames aren't attached)

- **Screen / flow** name
- **Frame range** (e.g. 274877–274890)
- **Trigger** — tap, load, success
- **What moves** — sheet, scrim, list rows, button
- **Feel** — snappy / spring / gentle, ~duration
- **Archetype** name

